# the effects' pool full (dsp/efx.h, 78 blocks): whoever holds memory keeps it, and a slot page offers only the effects
# that would find theirs there (engine_fits: its own memory counted free). PRESETS passes the others, the SEL list dims
# them ("no memory") and SEL refuses them; an effect set otherwise (a preset, a lock, MIDI, a project) without memory
# passes dry and its page says "not playing: memory full". A project loaded gives memory in a fixed order: FX I, FX II,
# Master FX, then the tracks, slot 1 then 2
wait 300
# FX II's chaos echo (32 blocks) beside FX I's delay (24): 22 left, no room for a track's delay (24)
param 12 s1x1 8
wait 100
expect fxroom1 1
expect fxroom2 1
spin ALGO 1
expect trk 2
tap FX
expect page Insert_1
# PRESETS stops at the catalog's ends (no wrapping round): from off, down, it stays off; from the reverb (the last,
# its plate, 12), up, it stays; down the catalog: rumble (2), then past the delay to autowah
turn PRESET -1
expect par2.ctype 0
param 2 ctype 18
wait 50
expect room2.1 1
turn PRESET 1
expect par2.ctype 18
turn PRESET -1
expect par2.ctype 17
wait 50
turn PRESET -1
expect par2.ctype 15
turn PRESET 1
expect par2.ctype 17
wait 50
expect room2.1 1
# the SEL list: the delay dimmed, "no memory"; SEL refuses it (the list stays, rumble kept)
tap SEL
expect listopen 1
rowval delay = no memory
rowval rumble = in use
row delay
listen
tap SEL
said no memory
expect listopen 1
expect par2.ctype 17
tap HOME
# track 4's plate (12) beside it: 8 left, the reverb too dimmed on track 2 (its rumble's 2 blocks not beside them)
param 4 ctype 18
param 4 cmix 100
wait 100
expect room4.1 1
tap SEL
rowval reverb = no memory
rowval delay = no memory
wait 2000
shot pool_list_full.png
tap HOME
param 4 ctype 0
wait 100
# FX I's delay off: its 24 blocks free, the delay offered on the track
param 11 ctype 0
wait 100
tap FX
expect page Insert_1
tap SEL
row delay
tap SEL
expect listopen 0
expect par2.ctype 16
wait 100
expect room2.1 1
# a preset with a delay (dub chord: Insert 2) onto track 3 where none is free (22 blocks left): it passes dry, its page
# says so, and the screen reader with it
preset 3 dub_chord
wait 100
expect par3.itype 16
expect room3.2 0
spin ALGO 1
expect trk 3
tap FX
turn SELECT 1
expect page Insert_2
wait 40
shot pool_not_playing.png
listen
where
said not playing: memory full
# FX I's delay set again (MIDI, a lock: the same): it waits too
param 11 ctype 16
wait 100
expect fxroom1 0
expect room2.1 1
# track 2's delay off: its blocks to FX I, waiting first (before track 3's)
param 2 ctype 0
wait 100
expect fxroom1 1
expect room3.2 0
# saved with track 2's delay holding, FX I waiting; loaded: FX I first (its delay), FX II, then the tracks: track 2's
# delay and track 3's wait now
param 2 ctype 16
param 11 ctype 0
wait 100
param 11 ctype 16
wait 100
expect room2.1 1
expect fxroom1 0
projsave 1
projsave 2
tap GLO
tap SEL
row PROJ 1
tap SEL
wait 200
expect projslot 1
expect par2.ctype 16
expect fxroom1 1
expect fxroom2 1
expect room2.1 0
expect room3.2 0
